  <h2>What shoppers actually browse</h2>
  <h3>Heritage tailoring (Burberry, Armani)</h3>
  <p>
    <strong>Burberry</strong> blazer rows emphasise plaid lining, button spacing, and lapel symmetry.
    QC focus: shoulder line, sleeve length, interior label fonts—structured pieces punish lazy approvals.
  </p>
  <h3>Streetwear hybrids (BAPE, Corteiz, Carhartt)</h3>
  <p>
    <strong>A Bathing Ape</strong> and <strong>Corteiz</strong> blazers trade on logo placement and unconventional cuts.
    Compare patch alignment and pocket symmetry in warehouse stills.
  </p>
  <h3>Technical &amp; workwear (CP Company, Carhartt)</h3>
  <p>
    <strong>CP Company</strong> and <strong>Carhartt</strong> rows blend utility fabrics with blazer silhouettes—verify lens badges and stitch density where applicable.
  </p>

  <h2>QC checklist for blazer rows</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Shoulders:</strong> padding symmetry, seam pitch, no visible puckering.</li>
    <li><strong>Lapel &amp; collar:</strong> roll, gorge height, button stance alignment.</li>
    <li><strong>Lining:</strong> pattern match at vents, colour consistency.</li>
    <li><strong>Buttons:</strong> engraving, spare button inclusion if promised.</li>
    <li><strong>Flat measurements:</strong> chest, shoulder width, sleeve—<a href="/blog/kakobuy-sizing-spreadsheet-apparel/">sizing guide</a>.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Use <a href="/blog/kakobuy-spreadsheet-qc/">warehouse QC</a> discipline—blazers are common retake categories.
  </p>

  <h2>Freight &amp; consolidation</h2>
  <p>
